  "extraction_status": "ready_for_resolution",
  "extraction_notes": "Text-layer table with vector rule lines. Column x-centres fixed from the header day labels; the mark matrix was re-derived mechanically by binning every pdftotext -bbox token to the rule-line-bounded cell it falls in, and diffed cell-for-cell against a visual read of the 200 dpi renders - no disagreement. Every internal vertical rule is present in every body row, so there are no merged body cells and no marks were distributed. The only merges are in the header: 'Treatment Period (Study Days)' across columns 3-21, and the 'Study Procedure' and 'Screening (D-42 to -2)' cells merged vertically across both header bands. Two full-width black redaction boxes on document page 11 conceal activity rows - see table_metadata.notes."
 },
 "table_metadata": {
  "table_number": 1,
  "table_type": "main_soa",
  "table_title": "Schedule of Activities (SoA)",
  "table_purpose": "Single schedule for all participants covering screening (Days -42 to -2), the inpatient treatment period (Study Days -1 to 18) and the follow-up / early discontinuation visit at Day 24 (± 2 days).",
  "page_start": 10,
  "page_end": 11,
  "notes": "Single SoA grid printed across document pages 10-11 under section heading '1.3. Schedule of Activities (SoA)'; the source prints no table number and no table title. The two-band column header (epoch band + study-day band) is reprinted verbatim at the top of page 11 and the body rows simply continue, so this is treated as ONE table (page_start 10, page_end 11) with the reprinted header de-duplicated, not as a main_soa + continuation pair. table_type main_soa: rows are procedures performed on participants, one population, one timeline, and it is the only grid in the excerpt. Label columns L=1 (Study Procedure); first data column is position 2; 21 data columns (2-22). SOURCE DEFECT - two solid black redaction boxes overprinted with the label 'CCI' cross the full width of the table on document page 11: one between the 'Genetic blood sample for screening' row and the 'Rosuvastatin PK samples' row (117 px tall at 200 dpi), one between 'Rosuvastatin PK samples' and 'Adverse event review' (82 px tall). Each conceals at least one activity row together with all of its marks; the number of concealed rows and their content cannot be determined, so no activity rows were emitted for them and row_position runs contiguously across the gaps. The footnote/abbreviation block for this table is printed on document page 12, which PAGEMAP.md declares to be beyond the SoA range; its text has been transcribed into annotations but page 12 is not included in page_start/page_end. Footnotes d, f and g are themselves redacted on that page."
 },
